 "icon": "farmings:vet_kit",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "para",
   "runs": [
    {
     "t": "Tame animals catch real diseases. They spread inside a barn, shed, coop, pig barn or stable, not between them. Nothing gory is shown, and by default no animal dies of disease: its health stops at a floor and it gives less."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "runs": [
    {
     "t": "What to watch for"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Coughing",
      "b": true
     },
     {
      "t": " and walking slowly: shipping fever (BRD) in cattle, strangles in horses."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "Head low",
      "b": true
     },
     {
      "t": ": any sick animal stands and walks with its head down."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "Limping",
      "b": true
     },
     {
      "t": ": foot rot (a short step on one foreleg, the head nodding). Clots in the milk: mastitis."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "Red diamond patches",
      "b": true
     },
     {
      "t": " on a pig: erysipelas."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "A "
     },
     {
      "t": "red band",
      "b": true
     },
     {
      "t": " on both hind legs: treated, and its milk or meat withheld."
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "An animal off its feed, lying down more, a hen that stops laying."
     }
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "runs": [
