  {
   "type": "para",
   "runs": [
    {
     "t": "Dirty bedding, litter or a full pit raises the risk for every animal housed on it. Cold piglets and chicks get scours and coccidiosis twice as often. Weaning a calf (8 weeks for dairy breeds) opens the shipping-fever window, as taming and moving do."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "runs": [
    {
     "t": "A healthier genome (the HEALTH score) halves the risk at 100 and doubles it at 0: a game rule, not a real-world figure."
    }
